# Template for the ssh config of the GPU training VM. `just ssh-config` fills it
# in from the site file (see site.env.example) and writes ./ssh_config, which is
# gitignored because it holds this site's addresses.
#
# `agx` is the ONE name for that machine. Its ProxyCommand (tools/agx-route)
# picks the direct or the jump-host route depending on which is alive, so
# nothing downstream -- ssh, scp, rsync, git, the Justfile -- ever needs to know
# which one is in use. See tools/agx-route for the probe and its cache.
#
# Used two ways:
#   * the Justfile passes -F <repo>/ssh_config explicitly, so `just` works
#     after `just ssh-config`;
#   * `just ssh-setup` also adds an Include line to ~/.ssh/config, after which
#     plain `ssh agx` / `scp x agx:` / `rsync agx:...` work with no flags.

Host agx
    HostName @AGX_DIRECT_HOST@
    User @AGX_USER@
    ProxyCommand @REPO@/tools/agx-route %h %p
    ServerAliveInterval 30
    ServerAliveCountMax 6

# The Proxmox hypervisor is reachable for host-level work, but its route is
# deliberately not recorded in this repo. Everything here goes through `agx`.
